   "CLOSE_TIP": "Found by a close spelling, not by the letters typed: a letter typed twice or missing, or one that Turkish and English write differently (h and kh, z and dh).",
   "WEAK_TIP": "The consonants typed are in this name, but its reading sounds different (Bayram and al-Barmaki are both b-r-m). Arabic is written without its short vowels, so consonants are matched first.",
   "UNREAD_TIP": "The consonants typed are in this name, and isnady has no reading of it to compare the vowels with, so it cannot say whether it sounds like what you typed."
  }
